{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1037338-the-science-of-empathy","id":1037338,"title":"The Science of Empathy","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-24T12:01:10-08:00","id":1037338,"title":"The Science of Empathy","content":"<a href=\"http://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0168010214002314\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.sciencedirect.com/science...68010214002314</a><br /> <br /> This is extremely fascinating and full of insights, I recommend reading this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T12:18:58-08:00","id":1037357,"title":"","content":"Semi-related story: When I was an undergrad, I presented at a student conference on <i>Beowulf</i>. After the four of us students gave our presentations, a literature professor in the audience who studied emotion in literary texts raised his hand during questioning to ask about the use of anachronistic terms before the labels for them existed (which was completely unrelated to anything any of us had been talking about). He was just like &quot;I'm going to make this student conference about me&quot;.<br /> <br /> So I was like, &quot;yeah, I disagree, but I think I see what you're arguing--it sounds like you think we shouldn't use anachronisms at all, so, for example, that we can't talk about gravity before 1687, and we shouldn't study emotion in texts published before we had a modern psychological understanding of emotions&quot;. <br /> <br /> And he got so mad at me and super embarrassed and that's the end of that story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T15:30:57-08:00","id":1037445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1037338-the-science-of-empathy?p=1037357#post1037357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And he got so mad at me and super embarrassed and that's the end of that story.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone who spent far too many years dealing with stuffy professors and wishing I could take them all down a few pegs, I salute you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T15:56:03-08:00","id":1037457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>hm8453a</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1037338-the-science-of-empathy?p=1037357#post1037357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Semi-related story: When I was an undergrad, I presented at a student conference on <i>Beowulf</i>. After the four of us students gave our presentations, a literature professor in the audience who studied emotion in literary texts raised his hand during questioning to ask about the use of anachronistic terms before the labels for them existed (which was completely unrelated to anything any of us had been talking about). He was just like &amp;quot;I'm going to make this student conference about me&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> So I was like, &amp;quot;yeah, I disagree, but I think I see what you're arguing--it sounds like you think we shouldn't use anachronisms at all, so, for example, that we can't talk about gravity before 1687, and we shouldn't study emotion in texts published before we had a modern psychological understanding of emotions&amp;quot;. <br /> <br /> And he got so mad at me and super embarrassed and that's the end of that story.</div> </div> </div> </div> Seems like you made a valid point, he had no reason to be embarrassed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T16:18:50-08:00","id":1037462,"title":"","content":"One particular part of what I linked to that I found really surprising how empathy can lead to less moral decisions, it's counter intuitive. <br /> <br /> For example you empathize highly with your best friend or a family member, so if you end up in a, situation where lives are at stake and you have choose between some one who empathize with vs 3 other people who you don't, you are more likely to save the person you empathize with instead of saving 3 other lives. Saving the 3 lives instead of the 1 is the more moral choice. <br /> <br /> Another interesting thing is how empathy appears to be at least in part your brain effectly running a simulation of what another person is experiencing. <br /> <br /> So if you see someone being hurt, you feel pain on some level, like roughly the same areas in your brain fire. <br /> <br /> I also found the different types of empathy interesting, and the whole Theory of Mind vs. Empathy, I plan on looking up more details on that. <br /> <br /> Another thing I liked is learning out to get people to empathize with someone who they normally wouldn't because they are, part of an group they not inclined to empathize with. <br /> <br /> And very relavant to another thread, Psychopaths are capable of Empathy, but it takes conscious effort, it doesn't happen automatically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:03:42-08:00","id":1037610,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'm surprised more people don't find this compelling and interesting and of value.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}